{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"mcr.microsoft.com/azurespheresdk","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:18:44.440Z","source":{"name":"Microsoft Artifact Registry","api":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/api/v1/catalog/azurespheresdk/details?reg=mar","page":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/en-us/product/azurespheresdk/azurespheresdk/about"},"readme":"## About\n\nThis repository contains the official container images for Microsoft Azure Sphere SDK. You can use Docker to run a standalone Linux container with the Azure Sphere SDK pre-installed. This image can also be used as a base for your own deployments. The image tag refers to the version of the SDK it contains.\n\n## Featured Tags\n\n`latest`: The image with the latest version of the Azure Sphere SDK.\n`docker pull mcr.microsoft.com/azurespheresdk:latest`\n\n## What is Azure Sphere SDK?\n\nThis is the SDK used to develop applications for Azure Sphere devices\n\nLearn more about Azure Sphere [here](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/services/azure-sphere)\n\nLearn more about the Azure Sphere SDK [here](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure-sphere/app-development/applications-overview)\n\n## Usage\n\n```\ndocker run -it mcr.microsoft.com/azurespheresdk:<version>\n```\nFor more instructions on how to use this image refer to [Use Azure Sphere SDK in a Docker container](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure-sphere/app-development/container-build).\n\n## Support\n\nIf you encounter any bugs with the tool or have other feedback please check out our support links [here](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure-sphere/resources/support).\n\n## License\n\n- Legal Notice: [Container License Information](https://aka.ms/mcr/osslegalnotice)","readmeBase":null,"publisher":{"name":"Microsoft","url":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/","official":true,"verified":true},"registered":null,"updated":"2025-05-02T05:34:51.6231776+00:00","categories":[],"keywords":[],"license":"MIT","links":[],"maintainers":[],"stats":{"pulls":null,"pullsText":"50K+","stars